

# ── Subject ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One line, imperative mood, no trailing period, under ~65 characters.
# Say the point of the change rather than the area it touched:
#
#   yes  Run the enforced rules in CI, not just on someone's laptop
#   no   ci changes
#
# No type prefixes (feat:, fix:, chore:) — this repo does not use them.
#
# ── Body ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Blank line, then why over what: the diff already shows what changed.
# Worth covering, when each applies —
#
#   · what was wrong, missing, or surprising before this change
#   · why this approach, over the one a reader would reach for first
#   · what bit you on the way, and would bite the next person
#   · anything deliberately left out, and why
#
# Wrap around 72 characters. Where docs/DECISIONS.md holds the reasoning,
# cite the ADR instead of restating it.
#
# Delete these comments or leave them — git strips every line starting
# with '#' before the message is saved.
